    <briefdescription>
<para>Already initialized error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1AlreadyInitializedError" kindref="compound">AlreadyInitializedError</ref> represents an error when attempting to initialize an object that has already been initialized (double-initialization).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>AlreadyInitializedError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Already<sp/>initialized&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>AlreadyInitializedError(&quot;Cannot<sp/>reinitialize<sp/>active<sp/>connection&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
